---
description: Nginx/OpenResty edge, Lua DFA, XDP BPF sync
globs: deploy/nginx/**, deploy/edge/**, internal/edge/**, cmd/edge-xdp/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Edge: OpenResty/nginx ingress + optional XDP L4 filter. Compliance map policy: `compliance.mdc`.

Listeners: :8180 HTTP/1.1; :443 H2/H3/H1.1 ALPN. Dev certs: `deploy/nginx/certs/generate-dev-certs.sh`.

L7 (`access-check.lua`): rate limit, circuit breaker, blacklist cache, body DFA (`edge-parse-dfa.lua`), per-campaign RL, proxy to tracker pool.

`TRACKER_INGRESS_SCHEMA` must match tracker config:

- `openrtb_3` (default): edge reads `request.item[0].id`
- native track: edge scans `campaign_id` — tracker `ParseTrackRequestJSON*` / vtproto

Shard selection must match Go `StaticSlotSharder`: `slot = crc32(campaign_id) & 1023` -> `slot_table[slot]`.

XDP: deny maps synced control outbox -> Redis shard-0 -> `cmd/edge-bpf-sync` -> `/sys/fs/bpf/`. Attach via `cmd/edge-xdp`. Control never writes kernel maps directly.

Related: `compliance.mdc`, `data-layer.mdc` shard-0 notes.
